00:04:48.109 --> 00:04:53.029
OpenAI is developing humanoid robots to take on Tesla and other robotics companies.

00:04:53.589 --> 00:04:54.629
Why Net News reports.

00:04:55.449 --> 00:04:59.889
Sam Altman has set a target for the first demonstration in 2027.

00:05:00.509 --> 00:05:05.269
The effort marks OpenAI's direct entry into hardware development alongside its existing

00:05:05.269 --> 00:05:06.549
AI software work.

00:05:06.549 --> 00:05:11.589
The timeline places open AI's first hardware showing one year ahead of several announced

00:05:11.589 --> 00:05:13.109
Tesla Optimus milestones.

00:05:14.999 --> 00:05:19.839
TSL aiming noted that development cycles have compressed from four years to 18 months

00:05:19.839 --> 00:05:20.939
across the industry.

00:05:21.519 --> 00:05:25.979
The shorter timelines force companies to skip durability validation steps that previously

00:05:25.979 --> 00:05:28.099
caught mechanical issues before launch.

00:05:28.739 --> 00:05:33.639
Regulators now require two winters and one summer of physical testing to offset the reduced

00:05:33.639 --> 00:05:34.719
internal validation.

00:05:34.719 --> 00:05:40.339
The post frames the change as a direct response to repeated field failures in recently launched

00:05:40.339 --> 00:05:40.839
vehicles.

00:05:41.259 --> 00:05:45.819
The move fast and break things approach works for mobile apps but not for vehicles carrying

00:05:45.819 --> 00:05:47.859
families at highway speeds, Ming said.

00:05:48.599 --> 00:05:53.519
The post supports regulatory moves that ban unproven features such as moving bed modes until

00:05:53.519 --> 00:05:55.199
full physical testing is complete.

00:05:55.819 --> 00:06:00.459
It argues that real-world durability cannot be validated through software simulation alone.

00:06:01.525 --> 00:06:08.605
Our Invest updated its model to project Tesla shares reaching levels implying nearly 1,100% growth

00:06:08.605 --> 00:06:15.865
from current prices by 2031. Benzinga reports. The forecast incorporates expected revenue from a

00:06:15.865 --> 00:06:21.945
potential Tesla SpaceX merger within five years. Kathy Woods firm highlighted Robotaxi and

00:06:21.945 --> 00:06:28.619
Optimus scaling as the primary drivers behind the valuation increase. The latest open source model

00:06:28.619 --> 00:06:34.239
assigns the majority of future value to a single business line reaching $4,400 per share

00:06:34.239 --> 00:06:40.559
by 2031. The model incorporates updated assumptions on robotaxi utilization rates and

00:06:40.559 --> 00:06:45.779
optimist deployment volumes. The file is available for public download and includes sensitivity

00:06:45.779 --> 00:06:53.246
tables for key input variables. Complex hand mechanisms continue to slow assembly timelines for the

00:06:53.246 --> 00:06:59.226
generation optimists, global sources reports. Workforce resistance at supplier sites has added

00:06:59.226 --> 00:07:04.746
further delays to scaling plans. Hand complexity exceeds initial engineering estimates by a

00:07:04.746 --> 00:07:10.206
significant margin. Supplier pushback centers on required precision tooling investments that have

00:07:10.206 --> 00:07:15.926
not yet been fully funded. Production of the third generation robot remains gated by both the intricate

00:07:15.926 --> 00:07:18.686
finger assemblies, and that labor resistance.

00:07:20.933 --> 00:07:26.893
Liner truck 3 already moves more than 22,000 pounds, confirming the hardware's load capacity

00:07:26.893 --> 00:07:28.513
before the freight bed was added.

00:07:29.033 --> 00:07:34.353
A truck that tops out at 12 miles per hour and runs on 28 miles of range can operate inside

00:07:34.353 --> 00:07:36.093
a controlled, flat route.

00:07:36.593 --> 00:07:41.333
In that tunnel, energy density and fast charging matter less than durability and simplicity.

00:07:41.953 --> 00:07:46.573
The tradeoff is that the same hardware cannot easily migrate to higher speed or longer

00:07:46.573 --> 00:07:52.553
range surface applications without redesign. So the shared part strategy works only inside a narrow

00:07:52.553 --> 00:07:58.113
operating window. Remote piloting from the Texas Operations Center removes the need for onboard

00:07:58.113 --> 00:08:03.653
driver interfaces or cabin safety systems that would add weight and cost on an open road vehicle.

00:08:04.393 --> 00:08:09.713
Repurposing automotive packs and drive units for underground freight changes the cost equation for both

00:08:09.713 --> 00:08:14.513
the vehicle maker and the tunneling company. The components now handle freight without a new

00:08:14.513 --> 00:08:18.393
powertrain design, cutting the marginal expense of each additional truck.

00:08:18.953 --> 00:08:24.013
That reuse also reduces the number of unique parts the supply chain must support, which

00:08:24.013 --> 00:08:27.473
matters when production volumes for the base vehicle remain the priority.

00:08:28.113 --> 00:08:32.813
Over repeated cycles, the shared hardware can lower the per-unit cost of every liner truck

00:08:32.813 --> 00:08:34.873
that rolls out of the same supplier base.

00:08:35.373 --> 00:08:40.133
For Tesla, the arrangement creates a small but steady internal demand signal for cells and

00:08:40.133 --> 00:08:43.073
motors that would otherwise sit in finished vehicle inventory.

00:08:43.073 --> 00:08:48.813
Over time, those steady, low variability orders can help smooth factory utilization even

00:08:48.813 --> 00:08:50.833
if external vehicle sales fluctuate.

00:08:51.333 --> 00:08:55.793
The current modification is an incremental step rather than a complete re-architecture.

00:08:56.313 --> 00:09:00.853
Whether the freight version finds paying external customers will determine if the reuse model

00:09:00.853 --> 00:09:04.653
becomes a repeatable margin lever or remains a niche demonstration.

00:09:05.233 --> 00:09:09.453
The valuation from September's funding round provides the runway to test that question

00:09:09.453 --> 00:09:10.573
at commercial volumes.

